00935 {\cf20 }\par
00936 {\cf20  Q: Where is the documentation?}\par
00937 {\cf20  A: This library is poorly documented at the moment and expects the user to be acquainted with C/C++.}\par
00938 {\cf20     - Run the examples/ applications and explore them.}\par
00939 {\cf20     - Read Getting Started (https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/wiki/Getting-Started) guide.}\par
00940 {\cf20     - See demo code in imgui_demo.cpp and particularly the ImGui::ShowDemoWindow() function.}\par
00941 {\cf20     - The demo covers most features of Dear ImGui, so you can read the code and see its output.}\par
00942 {\cf20     - See documentation and comments at the top of imgui.cpp + effectively imgui.h.}\par
00943 {\cf20     - 20+ standalone example applications using e.g. OpenGL/DirectX are provided in the}\par
00944 {\cf20       examples/ folder to explain how to integrate Dear ImGui with your own engine/application.}\par
00945 {\cf20     - The Wiki (https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/wiki) has many resources and links.}\par
00946 {\cf20     - The Glossary (https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/wiki/Glossary) page also may be useful.}\par
00947 {\cf20     - Your programming IDE is your friend, find the type or function declaration to find comments}\par
00948 {\cf20       associated with it.}\par
00949 {\cf20 }\par
