01008 {\cf20  Q: How can I help?}\par
01009 {\cf20  A: - Businesses: please reach out to "omar AT dearimgui DOT com" if you work in a place using Dear ImGui!}\par
01010 {\cf20       We can discuss ways for your company to fund development via invoiced technical support, maintenance or sponsoring contacts.}\par
01011 {\cf20       This is among the most useful thing you can do for Dear ImGui. With increased funding, we sustain and grow work on this project.}\par
01012 {\cf20       >>> See https://github.com/ocornut/imgui/wiki/Funding}\par
01013 {\cf20     - Businesses: you can also purchase licenses for the Dear ImGui Automation/Test Engine.}\par
01014 {\cf20     - If you are experienced with Dear ImGui and C++, look at the GitHub issues, look at the Wiki, and see how you want to help and can help!}\par
01015 {\cf20     - Disclose your usage of Dear ImGui via a dev blog post, a tweet, a screenshot, a mention somewhere etc.}\par
01016 {\cf20       You may post screenshot or links in the gallery threads. Visuals are ideal as they inspire other programmers.}\par
01017 {\cf20       But even without visuals, disclosing your use of dear imgui helps the library grow credibility, and help other teams and programmers with taking decisions.}\par
01018 {\cf20     - If you have issues or if you need to hack into the library, even if you don't expect any support it is useful that you share your issues (on GitHub or privately).}\par
